begin;
update public.character_profiles set tagline='Kajik’s bookshop · the clockwork stall · Rockside',heading='Page, the bookbinder',bio='Page had attended the Feylight Festival before and helped persuade the group to go. At Kajik’s Books, he promised to return in one year in exchange for a book. He later gave that book to Ethan, saying that curiosity should always be rewarded. At the cistern house, he kept a psychic link open while Legion approached the hive. After the courtyard escape, he helped the party reach the Hollow Heart and paid for their rooms. In session 26, he helped disguise Coy as a healer and told Ceridwen about his long connection to the Devereaux family and his promise to protect Simon.',mood='Helped the party reach the Hollow Heart',location='The Hollow Heart, Rockside · session 26',interests='Promised Kajik he would return in one year
Gave Ethan the trinket-making book
Maintained the psychic link in the cistern
Helped Coy prepare a healer disguise' where slug='page' and updated_at='2026-10-23 20:21:07.84264+00'::timestamptz returning slug;
update public.character_profiles set tagline='A story at the gate · a letter for the Copperfields',heading='Ceridwen’s stories and songs',bio='Ceridwen paid the party’s way into the Feylight Festival with a story. At the clockwork stall, she persuaded the ogre to accept an item of equal value in place of Ethan’s hundred years of service, then wrote a letter explaining the situation to his parents. At the cistern house, she played the campfire song Legion knew from the road. She later helped Coy dispel three magical trap nodes. In session 26, she contacted Stross by Sending and cast Zone of Truth while the party questioned the masked newcomer; the newcomer resisted the spell, so the account remained unconfirmed.',mood='Contacted Stross by Sending',location='The Hollow Heart, Rockside · session 26',interests='Told the story that opened the festival gate
Negotiated over Ethan’s debt
Wrote to Ernest and Elvira Copperfield
Played the campfire song in the cistern' where slug='ceridwen' and updated_at='2026-10-23 20:21:07.84264+00'::timestamptz returning slug;
update public.character_profiles set tagline='A clockwork bird · transmutation · Shape Water',heading='Coy’s field record',bio='Coy helped Ceridwen search for Ethan in Lobridge. At the festival, he bought the boy a clockwork bird and helped escort him back to his parents. At the cistern house, Coy detected transmutation magic resembling Legion’s magical presence and reminded Legion to remember themself during the meeting of swarms. He identified the toxin in a hive passage, helped Ceridwen dispel three trap nodes, and used Shape Water to wash the poison away. In session 26, he examined the masked newcomer’s injuries and planned to help injured people in Rockside while looking for information about Haven.',mood='Preparing to work as a healer in Rockside',location='The Hollow Heart, Rockside · session 26',interests='Gave Ethan a clockwork bird
Detected the cistern’s transmutation aura
Identified the poison made to kill swarms
Washed the passage with Shape Water' where slug='coy' and updated_at='2026-10-23 20:21:07.84264+00'::timestamptz returning slug;
update public.character_profiles set tagline='Rat-ions · clay tablets · the question of a name',heading='Legion and the other hive',bio='Legion offered a dried rat to the angry weasel on the road to the Feylight Festival. In the cistern house, they let their robed shape collapse, dropping clay tablets and runes, and joined the frightened swarm. They shared memories of Simon. When the new being asked who it was, Legion answered with images of sunrise and sunset and later spoke with it about travel and names. Legion also trapped the intruders’ entrance with caltrops. In session 26, they sealed the inn’s door with clay at night, supplied goodberries, and sent animal messengers to look for Hive and Selim.',mood='Sent animal messengers to find Hive and Selim',location='The Hollow Heart, Rockside · session 26',interests='Shared dried-rat rations with the weasel
Approached the hive with honey
Spoke with the new swarm about names
Protected the inn’s door with clay' where slug='legion' and updated_at='2026-10-23 20:21:07.84264+00'::timestamptz returning slug;
update public.character_profiles set tagline='A silver ticket · a traded memory · a globe’s map',heading='Simon Devereaux in the record',bio='Simon won a silver ticket at the festival’s hammer-and-bell booth. He paid Page’s messenger five silver and traded a memory to Alara for help finding Ethan. When Ethan tried to run from the clockwork stall, Simon caught him. Simon then studied the map on the broken brass globe, memorized it, and stopped with Ceridwen to draw it. Later in Latesa, the party identified a body in the Shave precinct morgue as Simon through its tattoos and a scar. Legion shared memories of him when trying to reach the frightened hive. This page records what the party witnessed and believed; it adds no offscreen account of his fate.',mood='Remembered by Legion in the cistern',location='The Shave precinct morgue · party’s last identification',interests='Won a silver ticket at the festival
Paid Page’s messenger five silver
Traded a memory to Alara
Memorized and drew the globe’s map' where slug='simon' and updated_at='2026-10-23 20:21:07.84264+00'::timestamptz returning slug;
update public.character_profiles set tagline='White and gold · citizenship for the hive',heading='Captain Selim Varek',bio='Stross brought Captain Selim Varek to the Bohun estate as a trusted ally assigned to protect and assist the party. The session recap describes his white-and-gold uniform and his belief in the goddess. After Legion explained that someone was stealing the hive’s larvae, Selim reasoned that the theft would be kidnapping if the hive were a citizen. In the courtyard fight, he attacked the militia spearman and later kicked the spear away from Page. Session 26 records Legion sending messengers to look for him; it does not establish a new location for him.',mood='Assigned to protect and assist the party',location='The Whites courtyard · last published scene',interests='Arrived with Stross at the Bohun estate
Accepted the party’s protection assignment
Considered citizenship for the hive
Turned the spear away from Page' where slug='selim' and updated_at='2026-10-23 20:21:07.84264+00'::timestamptz returning slug;
update public.character_profiles set tagline='The Whites courtyard · the Hollow Heart',heading='The masked gunslinger',bio='The party first encountered the gunslinger in the Whites courtyard: a small figure with two pistols, a wide-brimmed hat, a red-and-purple coat, and a clicking construct. She fired on the militia while Page held them with wind. In session 26, she introduced herself as Sandra Vale and claimed to work for the Devereaux family in pursuit of Simon’s killers. She resisted Ceridwen’s Zone of Truth, so the spell did not confirm her story. She said she needed her mask to survive and showed the party severe scarring. Coy examined the injury. Her stated name and allegiance are recorded claims, not an independent confirmation of her identity.',mood='Questioned by the party at the Hollow Heart',location='The Hollow Heart, Rockside · session 26',interests='Fired on the militia in the courtyard
Introduced herself as Sandra Vale
Said she needed the mask to survive
Allowed Coy to examine her injury' where slug='the-gunslinger' and updated_at='2026-10-23 20:21:07.84264+00'::timestamptz returning slug;
commit;
